    "eTitle": "Docker Compose v2 Multi-Service Topology & Port Exposure",
    "eDesc": "Construct a declarative Docker Compose v2 specification (`compose.yaml`) orchestrating a web application and an internal database. Demonstrate the critical distinction between published ports (`ports: ['3000:3000']`) bound to host network interfaces and internal exposed ports (`expose: ['5432']`) restricted exclusively to sibling containers on shared bridge networks. isPortReachableFromHost(serviceName, port) is true only when the service's ports list publishes that port ('3000:3000' publishes 3000; expose does not). canContainersCommunicate(a, b) is true when the two services share at least one network (services without networks are on 'default').",
    "eStarter": "class ComposeTopologyValidator {\n    config;\n    constructor(config) {\n        this.config = config;\n    }\n    isPortReachableFromHost(serviceName, targetPort) {\n        // Return true only if service publishes the target port to host\n        return false;\n    }\n    canContainersCommunicate(serviceA, serviceB) {\n        // Check if services share either the default network or any custom network\n        return false;\n    }\n}",
    "eHint": "Inspect whether any entry in the service ports array maps the container port to a host port using colon notation. For inter-service communication, check if both services are connected to a shared custom network or whether they both default to the project default network when no explicit networks are declared.",
    "eTest": "const validConfig = {\n    services: {\n        web: {\n            image: 'node:24-alpine',\n            ports: ['3000:3000'],\n            networks: ['frontend_net']\n        },\n        api: {\n            image: 'node:24-alpine',\n            networks: ['frontend_net', 'backend_net'],\n            expose: ['8080']\n        },\n        db: {\n            image: 'postgres:18-alpine',\n            expose: ['5432'],\n            networks: ['backend_net']\n        }\n    },\n    networks: {\n        frontend_net: {},\n        backend_net: {}\n    }\n};\nconst validator = new ComposeTopologyValidator(validConfig);\nif (!validator.isPortReachableFromHost('web', 3000))\n    throw new Error('Web port 3000 should be reachable from host');\nif (validator.isPortReachableFromHost('db', 5432))\n    throw new Error('DB port 5432 must NOT be reachable from host');\nif (!validator.canContainersCommunicate('web', 'api'))\n    throw new Error('Web and API should communicate via frontend_net');\nif (validator.canContainersCommunicate('web', 'db'))\n    throw new Error('Web and DB must be isolated across different networks');\nif (!validator.canContainersCommunicate('api', 'db'))\n    throw new Error('API and DB should communicate via backend_net');\nconsole.log('Day 100 Explorer tests passed successfully.');",
    "aTitle": "Compose Orchestrated Healthchecks & Custom Bridge Segmentation",
    "aDesc": "Implement a robust Compose startup orchestrator that prevents container startup race conditions. Model `depends_on` with `{ condition: 'service_healthy' }` linked to active container healthcheck probes (`pg_isready -U postgres`), ensuring dependent services are never launched until database engines are fully initialized. registerService(service) records it as 'starting'; markHealthy(name) makes it 'healthy'; canStartService(name, serviceList) is true only when every dependency with condition 'service_healthy' is healthy.",
    "aStarter": "class ComposeStartupCoordinator {\n    serviceHealth = new Map();\n    registerService(service) {\n        // Register service initial state\n    }\n    markHealthy(serviceName) {\n        // Transition service to healthy\n    }\n    canStartService(serviceName, serviceList) {\n        // Return true only if all depends_on condition requirements are satisfied\n        return false;\n    }\n}",
    "aHint": "Locate the target service in the service list and examine its dependencies map. If a dependency specifies the service_healthy condition, verify that the dependency service is currently marked healthy in the state map. If a dependency only requires service_started, confirm that the dependency is present.",
    "aTest": "const coordinator = new ComposeStartupCoordinator();\nconst services = [\n    {\n        name: 'db',\n        healthcheck: { test: ['CMD', 'pg_isready'], intervalMs: 500, timeoutMs: 200, retries: 3 }\n    },\n    {\n        name: 'api',\n        dependsOn: { db: { condition: 'service_healthy' } }\n    }\n];\ncoordinator.registerService(services[0]);\ncoordinator.registerService(services[1]);\nif (coordinator.canStartService('api', services))\n    throw new Error('API must not start while DB is only starting');\ncoordinator.markHealthy('db');\nif (!coordinator.canStartService('api', services))\n    throw new Error('API should be allowed to start once DB is healthy');\nconsole.log('Day 100 Architect tests passed successfully.');"
